quality_risk:
High if reached. For a GPT-6 max-effort worker, every text of at least 600 chars (task brief, AGENTS or developer context, earlier answers) arrives as its first 200 chars plus a marker. Getting the rest back needs all of these:
- the model chooses to call the tool;
- it copies all 24 hex chars exactly (upstream warns one wrong char fails);
- a live MCP link and a matching principal;
- the block is still within its TTL;
- full reads are at most 256 KiB.

The maintainer closed #6750 and #7538: markers reaching the model is by design. On CX the Responses restore drops the protocol note, so markers arrive explained only by the tool description. Tool outputs are exempt, so agent loops survive. The catalog label "Lossless" covers the store, not what the model sees.

Security: the durable tier writes verbatim prompt text (blocks up to 512 KB) to the SQLite table ccr_blocks for 24h by default. In keyless mode every lane shares one __anon__ principal.

